paperweight-plymouth (0.1.2-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add all four Catppuccin variant scripts: macchiato.script, latte.script,
    frappe.script, mocha.script — each with correct per-variant palette for
    background, wordmark (subtext0), and dots (mauve/lavender accent).
  * Add paperweight-plymouth-theme helper: copies selected variant script to
    paperweight.script and runs update-initramfs -u. Defaults to macchiato.
    Usage: sudo paperweight-plymouth-theme <variant>.
  * Add etc/sudoers.d/paperweight-plymouth: NOPASSWD for %sudo group so
    paperweight-theme can switch Plymouth silently alongside GRUB and gtkgreet.
  * debian/postinst: chmod 0440 sudoers drop-in and +x helper on configure.
  * debian/control: update description to mention all four variants.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Tue, 16 Jun 2026 00:00:02 +0000

paperweight-plymouth (0.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * postinst: add 'quiet splash' to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT if absent,
    then run update-grub. Without 'splash' the kernel never activates
    Plymouth and the theme never appears — this was the root cause of the
    boot splash not showing at all.
  * postrm: remove 'splash' from GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT on purge.
  * paperweight.script: replace pulsing wordmark with three-dot terminal
    sequence. Fixed 'paperweight' wordmark in $subtext0 (#a5adcb); three
    $lavender (#b7bdf8) dots below cycle opacity with 120° phase offsets
    to sequence left-to-right. Consistent with the keyboard-driven dev
    machine identity.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Tue, 16 Jun 2026 00:00:01 +0000

paperweight-plymouth (0.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Initial packaging. Catppuccin Macchiato Plymouth boot splash using the
    script plugin. Solid base background with pulsing centered label.
    Sets default Plymouth theme and rebuilds initramfs on install/remove.
  * debian/control: add plymouth-label to Depends — required for
    Image.Text() in the script plugin; without it the label silently fails.
  * paperweight.script: move logo SetX/SetY into refresh_callback so
    centering runs after the framebuffer is live, not at script load time.
    Remove no-op global angle declaration.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
